# UI Rebuild Rules — Emlak Master

Premium UI work is **composition rebuild**, not theme polish.

## Forbidden (incomplete UI work)

- Recoloring old screens only
- Adding gradients/glass wrappers without changing hierarchy
- Wrapping existing widgets in `PremiumCard` with same layout
- Incremental accent swaps (`ext.accent` → `champagneGold`) as the sole change
- Shipping debug badges/markers in release builds

## Required workflow (one screen at a time)

1. Inspect Figma/reference (`docs/PREMIUM_UI_IMPLEMENTATION_MAP.md`, Figma DNA tokens)
2. Map **visible sections** in reference vs current screen
3. Map **real providers/data** — no fake bindings
4. Rebuild **composition**: hierarchy, spacing, card structure, action placement
5. Preserve business logic, routes, providers, navigation
6. Verify all actions work (Functionality law)
7. Verify responsiveness: small iPhone, wide desktop, dark/light/system
8. Run `flutter analyze` + `flutter test`

A screen is **not complete** unless: visibly transformed, functionally wired, responsive, tested, performant.

## Premium UI standards

- Use shared kit: `PremiumCard`, `PremiumPageHeader`, `PremiumSectionHeader`, `PremiumMetricCard`, `PremiumSearchBar`, `PremiumShellBackdrop` (sparingly — not double-wrapped)
- Tokens: `PremiumColorTokens`, `PremiumThemeExtension`, `DesignTokens`, `AppTypography`
- Restraint: champagne gold for accent/hierarchy, not decoration spam

## Responsive rules

- `LayoutBuilder` / breakpoints for bento grids and split action rows
- Respect `DashboardLayoutTokens.shellScrollBottomPadding` for bottom nav clearance
- Text scale: test with enlarged system text; avoid fixed heights that clip

## Safe area & keyboard

- `SafeArea` on full-screen scaffolds; transparent scaffold + backdrop pattern OK
- Forms: keyboard inset, dismiss on tap outside, no trapped focus

## Bottom sheet discipline

- Use `showPremiumDraggableBottomSheet`, `PremiumBottomSheetHandle`, `PremiumSheetHeader`
- Dismiss: swipe + close affordance; no dead sheet actions

## Migration (UI)

- Refactor **in place** in the routed widget file
- **No** duplicate parallel screens or competing routes
- Do not change `app_router.dart` unless wiring fix is explicitly required

## Screen delivery checklist

For each rebuilt screen document: file changed, old vs new layout structure, visible differences, preserved providers, actions verified, QA notes (narrow/wide/dark/light).

